# Tech-debt agent session

Use when the user asks to implement the **next tech-debt issue**, `/next-debt`, or pastes output from `make debt-prompt`.

## Before coding

1. Run `make debt-next` (or read the issue URL the user provided).
2. If no eligible issue, stop and report why (all blocked or open PRs exist).
3. Read the issue body, parent epic (`## Parent`), `CONTEXT.md`, `docs/agents/implementation-workflow.md`, and relevant ADRs.
4. Load `.agents/skills/tdd/SKILL.md` — **vertical RED→GREEN slices only**; do not bulk-write tests then implement.

## Session rules

- **WIP=1** — only the picked issue in this session.
- Branch: `codex/issue-<number>-<short-slug>`.
- Scope: issue acceptance criteria only; no drive-by refactors.
- Skip `ready-for-human` issues (e.g. #63).

## Verification

| Change type | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Models / utils only | `make test` |
| UI, routing, persistence, E2E | `make check` |

Record exact commands and pass/fail in the PR.

## PR

- Title: concise, issue-focused
- Body: `Closes #<number>`, acceptance criteria checklist, verification section
- Link parent epic in PR description if helpful

## Out of scope

- Starting a second tech-debt issue in the same session
- Implementing blocked issues before blockers merge
- Product planner work (#29) unless that is the picked issue
